# Web environment template. See ../guides/CONNECTIONS.md for the shared map.
# Local: web/.env.local. Production: Vercel project docxy (https://docxy.app).
# Root .env configures the backend and is not loaded by Next.js in web/.
# Hosted changes require a redeployment; local edits do not sync automatically.

# ---- Database (Neon) --------------------------------------------------------
# Pooled connection string from the Neon console - the one containing `-pooler`.
# The same database also holds the docxy pipeline's tables; the dashboard's
# Better Auth tables live in a separate `auth` schema. See guides/DATABASE.md.
DATABASE_URL=


# ---- Session signing --------------------------------------------------------
# Required. openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Public origin, used to build OAuth callback URLs. Leave unset on localhost;
# set it behind a proxy, a tunnel, or in production.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://docxy.example.com
#
# Other origins that must also be able to sign in, comma-separated - a `www`
# you kept, an old platform alias. The canonical one above and the platform's
# own hostnames are trusted without being listed.
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://www.docxy.example.com

# ---- Social sign-in (both optional) -----------------------------------------
# Email + password works without either. A provider's button only appears once
# its credentials are set.

# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# https://github.com/settings/developers
# Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---- Dashboard ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the dashboard finds the docxy API server (`npm run serve` in the repo root).
# Production Vercel value: https://docxy-production.up.railway.app
# This is Railway tender-laughter/docxy; the refreshing-tenderness harness is retired.
DOCXY_API_URL=http://localhost:4317

# The shared secret the API expects, identical to DOCXY_API_TOKEN on the docxy
# server. This one fails quietly: without it every server-side read in
# src/lib/docxy.ts returns null and the dashboard renders its "offline" state,
# which looks like a pipeline that has never run rather than a missing variable.
DOCXY_API_TOKEN=

# How long the dashboard holds one live-update stream open, in seconds.
#
# The overview, activity and run pages subscribe to the pipeline's event feed
# and re-render themselves as a run progresses. Each stream is closed and
# reopened on this cadence, which is what re-checks the viewer's membership -
# a stream that never ends is a permission that is never asked about again.
#
# 55 fits inside the 60-second function ceiling available on every plan. Raise
# it only alongside `maxDuration` in src/app/api/docxy/[...path]/route.ts, and
# only to a limit the deployment actually has.
# DOCXY_STREAM_SECONDS=55

# Set to 0 to open /dashboard without signing in - how the demo runs.
# Leaving auth on with no OAuth provider configured above means the login page
# renders and none of its buttons work, so there is no way in at all.
# DOCXY_REQUIRE_AUTH=0

# There is no operator allowlist any more. Anyone who signs up and confirms
# their address gets an account, and authorization is by organization
# membership: every dashboard read names the caller's organization and the
# pipeline API refuses one that does not. DOCXY_ALLOWED_EMAILS is no longer
# read by anything - remove it from your deployment.

# ---- Email (Resend) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional mail: the signup confirmation link, the welcome that follows it,
# and organization invitations. All three are load-bearing rather than
# decorative.
#
# Registration is open exactly when both variables below are set, and closed
# otherwise. Without them a new account could not confirm its address, and an
# unconfirmed address can be claimed by whoever types it first - including for
# an organization invitation meant for its real owner. So the signup page closes
# itself instead of offering a form it cannot honour.
#
# Get a key at https://resend.com/api-keys. VERIFY THE SENDING DOMAIN FIRST:
# Resend accepts an unverified key happily and then refuses every individual
# message with a 403, which reads as "signups are open" and behaves as "nobody
# can ever confirm an account".
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# The domain all five product addresses are built on. Must be verified in
# Resend. This is the only email variable most deployments need.
# EMAIL_DOMAIN=docxy.app
#
# The five, and what each is for. Every one defaults to the mailbox shown, on
# EMAIL_DOMAIN, and is only worth setting to move a message somewhere unusual.
#
#   no-reply@    the verification link and organization invitations
#   onboarding@  the welcome note, with replies routed to support@
#   support@     where replies to product mail land
#   contact@     the address published for people who are not yet customers
#   arindam@     mail actually written by a person, not generated
#
# EMAIL_FROM=Docxy <no-reply@docxy.app>
# ONBOARDING_EMAIL_FROM=Docxy <onboarding@docxy.app>
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@docxy.app
# CONTACT_EMAIL=contact@docxy.app
# FOUNDER_EMAIL_FROM=Arindam Majumder <arindam@docxy.app>

# ---- Composio (organization integrations) -----------------------------------
# Server-side project API key from https://dashboard.composio.dev.
# Enables Slack, Notion, Linear, and Jira account connections in Integrations.
# Keep it private: never use a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. See guides/COMPOSIO.md.
# Provider accounts still need organization owner/admin authorization in the UI.
# Account connections do not yet enable notifications, publishing or issue workflows.
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# Optional custom auth configs, for your own OAuth app or restricted scopes.
# Managed authentication is used when these are absent.
# COMPOSIO_AUTH_CONFIG_SLACK=
# COMPOSIO_AUTH_CONFIG_NOTION=
# COMPOSIO_AUTH_CONFIG_LINEAR=
# COMPOSIO_AUTH_CONFIG_JIRA=

# ---- GitHub App (install flow) ----------------------------------------------
# The App's public slug, used to build the install link:
#   https://github.com/apps/<slug>/installations/new
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=docxy-bot

# The App's OWN OAuth credentials - not GITHUB_CLIENT_ID/SECRET above, which are
# for signing in. Required for every installation: the callback verifies access
# before connecting it, including when OAuth during installation is disabled.
# Set the App's Callback URL to https://<app-origin>/api/github/callback and
# Setup URL to https://<app-origin>/api/github/installed. Register the localhost
# callback separately when testing locally. Both install modes are supported.
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=


# ---- Billing (Dodo Payments) -------------------------------------------------
# Absent, the dashboard runs with payments switched off: Free entitlements still
# work, the pricing page still renders, and nothing offers a checkout. Nothing
# here is read at build time.
#
# Which Dodo account this deployment talks to. Defaults to test_mode when unset,
# because an unset variable should fail to take real money, not succeed at it.
# DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT=test_mode

# Server-side API key for that environment, from the Dodo dashboard.
# DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY=

# The webhook endpoint's signing secret. Deliveries are refused without it, and
# a refused delivery is the right outcome: an unverified event is a stranger
# claiming somebody paid.
# DODO_PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_KEY=

# One recurring product per paid plan, created separately in test and live mode
# with no trial and a monthly cadence. Prices and allowances come from the
# catalog in src/billing/catalog.ts; these only say what Dodo calls each one.
# DODO_PRODUCT_PRO_MONTHLY=
# DODO_PRODUCT_TEAM_MONTHLY=

# The recurring add-on billed per Team seat beyond the five the base package
# includes. Its quantity is derived on the server, never sent by a browser.
# DODO_PRODUCT_TEAM_SEAT=

# Purchases are off until this is set, separately from event processing: a
# subscription bought yesterday still renews, cancels and refunds while new
# purchases are paused.
# DOCXY_BILLING_ENABLED=1

# Free enrolment is its own switch and its own budget, because Free execution is
# an acquisition expense with a monthly ceiling (guides/PRICING.md). Pausing new
# grants must not disturb the ones already made.
# DOCXY_FREE_ENROLLMENT_ENABLED=1
# DOCXY_FREE_BUDGET_USD=105
